    <param.summary>A competion based app to encourage users to design the best PI compensator and feedforward for optimum lap times.</param.summary>
    <param.description>This resource provides an interactive app file (MATLAB virtual laboratory) which investigates the behaviour of a racing car on a track. Specifically the user can investigate the efficacy of a PI compensator for steering control, a PI compensator for speed control and the efficacy of feedforward of track information. Users can also change the desired maximum speed and constraints on steering wheel movements. The aim is to find the tuning which gives the optimum behaviour (lap time with minimum wear and tear and fuel).</param.description>
